      "side": 1,
      "message": "This approach of\n```\nextern \"C\" fn foo(...) -\u003e AvbIOResult { try_foo(...).into() }\n\nfn try_foo(...) -\u003e Result\u003c(), AvbIOError\u003e { ... }\n```\nwhere you can use `?` in `try_foo` while still returning `AvbIOResult` in the C-compatible functions is neat.",
